Gifscythe License Notice
========================

Gifscythe — the first-party code (GUI, control layer, CLI, web client, and
any future C# shell) — is distributed under the Microsoft Public License
(Ms-PL). See COPYING.ms-pl for the full license text.

Revision note (2026-09-14, S18 — owner decision OD-09 = b): the UI was
previously *intended* GPLv3, as the base for a Caesium-derived UX. That base
was never incorporated — no Caesium file ever entered the product tree — and
the owner relicensed the first-party code to Ms-PL to match the ScreenToGif
reference fork (also Ms-PL), whose files may now be adapted here with their
notices retained. No third-party code is in the relicensed tree, so no
third-party permission was needed for the relicense itself.

UI look-and-feel is rebuilt from open parts (system fonts and MIT/Apache
licensed icon sets), not from any proprietary or GPL asset. Layout and
workflow inspiration (XNConvert-style) uses no third-party files.

The bundled gifsicle engine is a SEPARATE PROGRAM, invoked as a subprocess.
gifsicle is Copyright (C) Eddie Kohler and is licensed under the GNU General
Public License, Version 2 ONLY. See COPYING.gifsicle and
reference_code/gifsicle/COPYING.

Because gifsicle is GPL v2-only, it is NEVER linked into the Gifscythe binary.
Shipping gifsicle alongside Gifscythe requires redistributing its license text
(COPYING.gifsicle) and offering its corresponding source (the reference_code/
gifsicle tree, or upstream https://github.com/kohler/gifsicle).

Qt is used under the LGPL v3 (or a commercial Qt license, if you have one).

For the full GPLv2 text covering the engine, see COPYING.gifsicle.
For the full Ms-PL text covering the first-party code, see COPYING.ms-pl.
Rationale and copying rules: docs/legal/ (WHY_MSPL.md, COPYING_RULES.md).
